WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.817
Sunlight falls on a rooftop,

2
00:00:01.817 --> 00:00:03.025
and a fan in the room below

3
00:00:03.025 --> 00:00:04.383
starts to turn.

4
00:00:04.383 --> 00:00:06.819
Not one moving part made that happen.

5
00:00:07.219 --> 00:00:09.251
When sunlight reaches a solar cell,

6
00:00:09.251 --> 00:00:11.399
some of it bounces off and some

7
00:00:11.399 --> 00:00:13.140
passes through.

8
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.578
Only the light that is absorbed makes

9
00:00:15.578 --> 00:00:16.714
electricity.

10
00:00:17.114 --> 00:00:20.016
A cell is made of a semiconductor.

11
00:00:20.016 --> 00:00:23.023
Absorbed light knocks electrons free;

12
00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.125
they gather at the front surface,

13
00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:27.064
and metal contacts collect them as a

14
00:00:27.064 --> 00:00:28.002
current.

15
00:00:28.403 --> 00:00:29.750
Many cells make a panel,

16
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.549
also called a module.

17
00:00:31.549 --> 00:00:33.465
Panels wired together make an array,

18
00:00:33.465 --> 00:00:35.669
from a rooftop to a solar park.

19
00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.799
There is one catch.

20
00:00:37.799 --> 00:00:39.598
Cells make direct current,

21
00:00:39.598 --> 00:00:42.071
but homes and the grid use alternating

22
00:00:42.071 --> 00:00:43.337
current.

23
00:00:43.337 --> 00:00:46.483
A box called an inverter converts one

24
00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:47.700
into the other.

25
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.062
Large solar farms are so big that

26
00:00:50.062 --> 00:00:51.757
weather satellites can see them flash in

27
00:00:51.757 --> 00:00:52.951
the sunlight.

28
00:00:53.351 --> 00:00:54.361
For GS Three,

29
00:00:54.361 --> 00:00:55.708
remember the chain:

30
00:00:55.708 --> 00:00:57.391
light, free electrons,

31
00:00:57.391 --> 00:00:58.993
direct current, inverter,

32
00:00:58.993 --> 00:01:00.571
alternating current.

